n6. Multiply 70 by 5:\n   ```\n   70 \u00d7 5 = 350\n   ```\n\n7. Multiply 8 by 400:\n   ```\n   8 \u00d7 400 = 3200\n   ```\n\n8. Multiply 8 by 30:\n   ```\n   8 \u00d7 30 = 240\n   ```\n\n9. Multiply 8 by 5:\n   ```\n   8 \u00d7 5 = 40\n   ```\n\nNow, we add all these partial products together:\n```\n360000 + 27000 + 4500 + 28000 + 2100 + 350 + 3200 + 240 + 40 = 421430\n```\nThis confirms that the product of 978 and 435 is indeed 421430.\n</answer>.<|User|>This is very helpful. Can you provide an example of how to use the standard algorithm to multiply 978 by 435, but this time show the step-by-step process?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c><think>.\nCertainly! The standard algorithm for multiplication involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's go through the step-by-step process for multiplying 978 by 435.\n\n1. Write the numbers one above the other, aligning the digits by place value:\n```\n  978\n\u00d7 435\n```\n\n2. Multiply 978 by the units digit of 435 (which is 5):\n```\n  978\n\u00d7   5\n-----\n 4890\n```\n   - Multiply 8 by 5: \\(8 \\times 5 = 40\\). Write down 0 and carry over 4.\n   - Multiply 7 by 5: \\(7 \\times 5 = 35\\). Add the carried over 4: \\(35 + 4 = 39\\). Write down 9 and carry over 3.\n   - Multiply 9 by 5: \\(9 \\times 5 = 45\\). Add the carried over 3: \\(45 + 3 = 48\\). Write down 48.\n\n3. Multiply 978 by the tens digit of 435 (which is 30, or 3 with a zero appended):\n```\n  978\n\u00d7  30\n-----\n 29340\n```\n   - Multiply 8 by 30: \\(8 \\times 30 = 240\\). Write down 240.\n   - Multiply 7 by 30: \\(7 \\times 30 = 210\\). Write down 210.\n   - Multiply 9 by 30: \\(9 \\times 30 = 270\\). Write down 270.\n\n4. Multiply 978 by the hundreds digit of 435 (which is 400, or 4 with two zeros appended):\n```\n  978\n\u00d7 400\n-----\n391200\n```\n   - Multiply 8 by 400: \\(8 \\times 400 = 3200\\). Write down 3200.\n   - Multiply 7 by 400: \\(7 \\times 400 = 2800\\). Write down 